# Setting Up LiveKit Dashboard MCP in Claude Code

## Prerequisites

- Claude Code installed
- An MCP API key from your LiveKit Dashboard
- Your public IP address whitelisted on the dashboard

---

## Step 1: Create `.mcp.json` in your project root

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "livekit-dashboard": {
      "type": "streamable-http",
      "url": "https://<YOUR_DASHBOARD_URL>/mcp",
      "headers": {
        "Authorization": "Bearer <YOUR_API_KEY>"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

> **Note:** The native MCP connection may not work yet due to a server-side Accept header issue. The config is there for when it's fixed. For now, we use a curl workaround (see Step 2).

---

## Step 2: Create `CLAUDE.md` in your project root

This tells Claude Code how to communicate with the MCP via curl:

````markdown
# LiveKit Dashboard MCP

The LiveKit Dashboard MCP server is available at `https://<YOUR_DASHBOARD_URL>/mcp`.
The native streamable-http connection does not work yet. Use curl to call the MCP directly.

## How to call any MCP tool

```bash
curl -s -X POST https://<YOUR_DASHBOARD_URL>/mcp \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer <YOUR_API_KEY>" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "Accept: application/json, text/event-stream" \
  -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"TOOL_NAME","arguments":{...}}}'
```

Always include all three headers. Responses come as SSE `data:` lines containing JSON-RPC results.

## Available Tools

### Agent Management
- `list_agents` — List all agents (no args)
- `get_agent` — Get agent config (agent_id)
- `get_agent_by_slug` — Look up by slug (slug)
- `create_agent` — Create agent (name, slug required)
- `update_agent_instructions` — Update prompt (agent_id, instructions)
- `update_agent_config` — Update any field (agent_id required, all others optional)
- `delete_agent` — Delete agent (agent_id)
- `duplicate_agent` — Copy agent (agent_id)
- `start_agent` / `stop_agent` — Start/stop agent (agent_id)

### Call History
- `list_calls` — List calls (optional: days, direction, agent_name, search, page, per_page)
- `get_call_detail` — Call details + AI summary (call_id)
- `get_call_transcript` — Transcript (call_id)
- `get_call_statistics` — Aggregated stats (no args)

### Analytics
- `get_overview` — Dashboard KPIs (no args)
- `get_call_volume` — Volume with comparison (days)
- `get_agent_performance` — Per-agent stats (days)
- `get_sentiment` — Sentiment trends (days)
- `get_latency` — Latency percentiles (days)

### Telephony
- `list_dispatch_rules` — SIP dispatch rules (no args)
- `list_sip_trunks` — All SIP trunks (no args)
- `list_active_rooms` — Active rooms (no args)
- `create_sip_inbound_trunk` — Create inbound trunk (name required; numbers, allowed_addresses, auth, number_format optional)
- `update_sip_inbound_trunk` — Partial update (sip_trunk_id required; omitted fields keep their current values)
- `create_sip_outbound_trunk` — Create outbound trunk (name, address required; transport, trunk_type pstn/pbx, auth, caller-ID numbers optional)
- `update_sip_outbound_trunk` — Partial update (sip_trunk_id required)
- `delete_sip_trunk` — Delete a trunk, inbound or outbound (sip_trunk_id)
- `create_dispatch_rule` — Route inbound calls to an agent (name required; trunk_ids, agent_slug, rule_type, auto_record, time_profile_id optional)
- `update_dispatch_rule` — Partial update; existing agent/trunk/recording settings are preserved (sip_dispatch_rule_id required)
- `delete_dispatch_rule` — Delete a dispatch rule (sip_dispatch_rule_id)

### Chatbot (Web Chat) Agents
- `list_chatbot_agents` — List website chatbot agents (no args)
- `get_chatbot_agent` — Full chatbot config incl. widget, avatar, and SMS/WhatsApp settings (agent_id)
- `create_chatbot_agent` — Create a chatbot agent (name required)
- `update_chatbot_agent` — Partial update; supports nested patches for widget_config, mem0_config, avatar_config, and sms_config (agent_id required)
- `delete_chatbot_agent` — Delete a chatbot agent (agent_id)

### Diagnostics & Help
- `get_agent_logs` — Agent logs (agent_id, lines)
- `get_dashboard_help` — Help by topic (topic)
- `get_agent_config_reference` — Config reference for voice agents, chatbot agents, and SIP management (no args)
- `get_admin_guide` — Full admin guide (no args)

This is not the full list — call `{"method":"tools/list"}` to discover every available tool (tool configuration, knowledge base, memory, webhook tools, diagnostics, and more).
````

---

## Step 3: Create `.claude/settings.local.json` in your project root

```json
{
  "permissions": {
    "allow": [
      "Bash(curl * https://<YOUR_DASHBOARD_URL>/mcp*)"
    ]
  }
}
```

Replace `<YOUR_DASHBOARD_URL>` with your actual dashboard domain.

This allows Claude Code to make curl calls to the MCP without prompting every time.

---

## Step 4: Whitelist your IP address

When creating your MCP API key on the dashboard, click the **"Use My IP"** button to automatically add your current IP address to the allowlist.

If your IP changes later, you'll need to update it in the API key settings on the dashboard.

---

## Step 5: Use it

Open Claude Code from your project directory and just ask:

- "List my LiveKit agents"
- "Show call stats for the last 7 days"
- "Get the transcript for the latest call"
- "Update the greeting on agent X"

Claude Code reads the `CLAUDE.md` automatically and knows how to call the MCP.

---

## Placeholders to replace

| Placeholder | Replace with | Example |
|---|---|---|
| `<YOUR_DASHBOARD_URL>` | Your dashboard domain (no `https://`) | `dashboard.example.com` |
| `<YOUR_API_KEY>` | Your MCP API key from the dashboard | `sk-mcp-abc123...` |

---

## Troubleshooting

| Issue | Fix |
|---|---|
| **403 — IP not in allowlist** | Update your IP in the API key settings on the dashboard |
| **401 — Unauthorized** | Check your API key is correct |
| **406 — Not Acceptable** | Make sure `Accept: application/json, text/event-stream` header is included |
| **Getting prompted for every curl** | Check `settings.local.json` has the wildcard permission |
| **Claude doesn't know about MCP** | Make sure you're in the directory with `CLAUDE.md` |
